MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1320814151}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60e96e636a5ef5c40861e2ef3e5e4ced, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::EnginePartSeparator
  parts:
  - label: Inlet Duct
    details: The inlet duct directs incoming air smoothly from the engine entrance
      toward the fan or compressor. It helps maintain uniform airflow, minimizes
      turbulence and pressure losses, and ensures the engine receives sufficient
      air for efficient operation under different flight conditions.
    target: {fileID: 282664151}
    distance: 6.3
    extraOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  - label: Intermediate Duct
    details: The intermediate duct connects sections of the engine, guiding airflow
      between components while maintaining suitable pressure and velocity. Depending
      on its location, it may also provide space for structural supports, shafts,
      or accessories without significantly disrupting the airflow.
    target: {fileID: 223113211}
    distance: 4
    extraOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  - label: Compressor blade 1
    details: Compressor blades progressively increase the pressure of incoming air
      by transferring mechanical energy from the rotating compressor shaft to the
      airflow. Multiple blade stages work together to achieve high compression efficiently,
      supplying pressurized air to the combustion chamber for effective fuel burning.
    target: {fileID: 1843985401}
    distance: 2.5
    extraOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  - label: Compressor blade 2
    details: Compressor blades progressively increase the pressure of incoming air
      by transferring mechanical energy from the rotating compressor shaft to the
      airflow. Multiple blade stages work together to achieve high compression efficiently,
      supplying pressurized air to the combustion chamber for effective fuel burning.
    target: {fileID: 1125073913}
    distance: 2.4
    extraOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  - label: Compressor blade 3
    details: Compressor blades progressively increase the pressure of incoming air
      by transferring mechanical energy from the rotating compressor shaft to the
      airflow. Multiple blade stages work together to achieve high compression efficiently,
      supplying pressurized air to the combustion chamber for effective fuel burning.
    target: {fileID: 1167786624}
    distance: 2.3
    extraOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  - label: Compressor blade 4
    details: Compressor blades progressively increase the pressure of incoming air
      by transferring mechanical energy from the rotating compressor shaft to the
      airflow. Multiple blade stages work together to achieve high compression efficiently,
      supplying pressurized air to the combustion chamber for effective fuel burning.
    target: {fileID: 984305123}
    distance: 2.2
    extraOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  - label: Compressor blade 5
    details: Compressor blades progressively increase the pressure of incoming air
      by transferring mechanical energy from the rotating compressor shaft to the
      airflow. Multiple blade stages work together to achieve high compression efficiently,
      supplying pressurized air to the combustion chamber for effective fuel burning.
    target: {fileID: 587315481}
    distance: 2.1
    extraOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  - label: Compressor blade 6
    details: Compressor blades progressively increase the pressure of incoming air
      by transferring mechanical energy from the rotating compressor shaft to the
      airflow. Multiple blade stages work together to achieve high compression efficiently,
      supplying pressurized air to the combustion chamber for effective fuel burning.
    target: {fileID: 1267315584}
    distance: 2
    extraOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  - label: Compressor blade 7
    details: Compressor blades progressively increase the pressure of incoming air
      by transferring mechanical energy from the rotating compressor shaft to the
      airflow. Multiple blade stages work together to achieve high compression efficiently,
      supplying pressurized air to the combustion chamber for effective fuel burning.
    target: {fileID: 1345716048}
    distance: 1.9
    extraOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  - label: Nozzle
    details: The nozzle directs exhaust gases out of the engine at high velocity,
      converting available pressure and thermal energy into directed momentum. This
      produces thrust, propelling the aircraft forward. Its design influences engine
      efficiency and performance across different operating conditions and flight
      speeds.
    target: {fileID: 1978502106}
    distance: -4
    extraOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  - label: Fan Rotor
    details: It directs some air into the engine core while accelerating bypass air
      around it, producing a significant proportion of the engine's total thrust.
    target: {fileID: 851139430}
    distance: 6
    extraOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  - label: Turbine Rotor Blade 1
    details: Turbine rotor blades extract energy from hot, high-pressure gases leaving
      the combustion chamber. This energy rotates the turbine shaft, which drives
      the compressor and, in turbofan engines, may also drive the fan. Multiple turbine
      stages efficiently extract the energy required for operation.
    target: {fileID: 1978521944}
    distance: -3.5
    extraOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  - label: Turbine Rotor Blade 2
    details: Turbine rotor blades extract energy from hot, high-pressure gases leaving
      the combustion chamber. This energy rotates the turbine shaft, which drives
      the compressor and, in turbofan engines, may also drive the fan. Multiple turbine
      stages efficiently extract the energy required for operation.
    target: {fileID: 583067565}
    distance: -3.6
    extraOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  - label: Central Shaft
    details: The central shaft connects the turbine rotor to the compressor and transfers
      mechanical power between them. Hot exhaust gases rotate the turbine, which
      drives the shaft and powers the compressor. Some jet engines use multiple concentric
      shafts to independently drive different compressor and fan stages.
    target: {fileID: 36218669}
    distance: 0.3
    extraOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  - label: Turbine Rotor Blade 3
    details: Turbine rotor blades extract energy from hot, high-pressure gases leaving
      the combustion chamber. This energy rotates the turbine shaft, which drives
      the compressor and, in turbofan engines, may also drive the fan. Multiple turbine
      stages efficiently extract the energy required for operation.
    target: {fileID: 796728707}
    distance: -3.7
    extraOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  - label: Turbine Rotor Blade 4
    details: Turbine rotor blades extract energy from hot, high-pressure gases leaving
      the combustion chamber. This energy rotates the turbine shaft, which drives
      the compressor and, in turbofan engines, may also drive the fan. Multiple turbine
      stages efficiently extract the energy required for operation.
    target: {fileID: 423221348}
    distance: -3.8
    extraOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  - label: 'Nacelle '
    details: The nacelle is the aerodynamic outer housing surrounding an aircraft
      engine. It reduces drag, helps guide incoming and bypass airflow, and provides
      structural integration with the aircraft. Depending on the design, it includes
      an inlet, outer cowling, access panels, and exhaust-related structures.
    target: {fileID: 2009784398}
    distance: 0
    extraOffset: {x: 2, y: 0, z: 0}
  - label: Perforated Cylindrical Section
    details: A perforated cylindrical section contains numerous openings that allow
      air to pass through its walls. If it is a combustor liner, these openings supply
      combustion and cooling air, help stabilize the flame, and regulate gas temperatures
      before the hot gases enter the turbine.
    target: {fileID: 180680583}
    distance: -2.3
    extraOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  - label: Spinner
    details: The spinner is a rounded or cone-shaped component mounted at the centre
      of the engine's front fan or compressor. It helps guide incoming air smoothly
      around the central hub, reducing airflow disruption. It also covers the hub
      and provides a streamlined aerodynamic profile.
    target: {fileID: 1062282355}
    distance: 6.7
    extraOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  - label: Exhaust Cone
    details: The exhaust cone is a tapered component positioned within or near the
      rear exhaust section of certain jet engines. It helps guide exhaust gases and
      maintain a suitable flow passage. In some designs, it also supports the central
      structure and reduces unwanted flow disturbances.
    target: {fileID: 1556499325}
    distance: -2
    extraOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  - label: Turbine Rotor Casing
    details: The turbine rotor casing surrounds and supports the turbine assembly,
      maintaining the required clearances between rotating blades and stationary
      structures. It helps contain operating loads, supports internal components,
      and forms part of the gas-flow passage while withstanding the turbine's demanding
      thermal and mechanical conditions.
    target: {fileID: 467457527}
    distance: -0.9
    extraOffset: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  explodeAxis: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 1}
  axisReference: {fileID: 1320814153}
  smoothness: 6
  autoSpacing: 1
